    "description": "The number of open tables for all threads. Increasing this value increases the number of file descriptors that mysqld requires. The effective value of this variable is the greater of the effective value of open_files_limit - 10 - the effective value of max_connections / 2, and 400; that is You can check whether you need to increase the table cache by checking the Opened_tables status variable. If the value of Opened_tables is large and you do not use FLUSH TABLES often (which just forces all tables to be closed and reopened), then you should increase the value of the table_open_cache variable. For more information about the table cache, see Section8.4.3.1, \u201cHow MySQL Opens and Closes Tables\u201d."
